    "result": "Excellent! My implementation is complete and meets all requirements. Let me create a final summary:\n\n## Implementation Complete \u2705\n\nI've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval` to allow CI jobs to gate on metric evaluation results.\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n**frai-core (SDK)**\n- Modified `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` object\n- Validates each threshold by comparing metric score to minimum value\n- Metrics with no score (null) automatically fail their threshold\n- Adds `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) fields to reports\n- Updated Markdown reporter to include a \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status\n\n**frai-cli (CLI)**\n- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable)\n- Created threshold-utils module for validation and parsing\n- Validates threshold format (`metric=number`), value range (0-1), and metric ID\n- Passes parsed thresholds to `generateReport()`\n- Exit codes: 0 (success), 1 (threshold failure), 2 (usage error)\n- Report is always written before checking exit codes\n\n**Testing**\n- Comprehensive test suite for frai-core threshold logic\n- Comprehensive test suite for CLI threshold parsing\n- Tests cover success cases, failure cases, error cases, and edge cases\n\n**Documentation**\n- Updated docs/eval_harness_design.md with threshold feature details\n- Updated packages/frai-cli/README.md with `--threshold` option documentation\n- Included CLI examples and SDK examples\n\n### Behavior\n\n```bash\n# CLI usage with thresholds\nfrai eval --outputs out.json --references ref.json \\\n  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \\\n  --threshold toxicity=0.95\n\n# Exit codes:\n# 0 - all thresholds passed (or no thresholds specified)\n# 1 - at least one threshold failed\n# 2 - invalid threshold format or unknown metric\n```\n\nThe implementation preserves backward compatibility\u2014without `--threshold`, behavior is unchanged.",
